WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.119 --> 00:00:03.920
If it's for performance purely, it would

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.159
be smarter to drop out.

00:00:06.159 --> 00:00:07.639
But that's not who I am.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.840
I like to do things not only because I

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.559
want to try to win the race,

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:15.800
but it's more about trying to explore my

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.719
body physiology, training and all that.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.559
And injuries and

00:00:19.559 --> 00:00:22.960
problems are part of our lives.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.880
It gives me a lot of freedom to

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:25.960
experiment about those things,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:28.280
trying to say, "Okay, let's go to a race

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.840
injured and see how

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.519
we can deal with things.

00:00:31.519 --> 00:00:33.719
And I have done that for all my career.

00:00:37.039 --> 00:00:38.079
So tell me.

00:00:39.679 --> 00:00:40.880
It's alright.

00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:44.480
Yesterday I did 90k running

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:49.159
And I don't feel more

00:00:49.159 --> 00:00:52.960
pain or the muscles are okay.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.280
And it's more when I go fast.

00:00:59.119 --> 00:01:00.199
And downhill, uphill?

00:01:00.679 --> 00:01:01.679
downhill

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.000
So do you feel that it

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.280
has been, that it's milder?

00:01:09.039 --> 00:01:10.199
Yeah, it's milder for sure.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.639
And last week you said you did 70k?

00:01:16.639 --> 00:01:17.840
Yeah, 70k.

00:01:20.239 --> 00:01:23.000
And then this week I did on Monday 50k

00:01:26.199 --> 00:01:28.239
And yesterday 90k.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.800
Are we heading in the right direction?

00:01:33.199 --> 00:01:35.000
I think it's good.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:36.960
Then after the race, I don't know.

00:01:37.199 --> 00:01:40.000
Well, after the race it's something else.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.639
Yeah.

00:01:41.599 --> 00:01:43.000
What's your plan next week?

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:44.719
No, no, it's very easy.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:46.559
When do you travel?

00:01:46.559 --> 00:01:47.960
I'll travel tomorrow.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.679
I think I will see how I feel tomorrow

00:02:12.679 --> 00:02:16.960
but so far it's been a good test.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.760
So there is hope.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.360
There is hope,

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.519
There is always hope.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:34.800
Friday evening, one week before the race.

00:02:36.159 --> 00:02:38.960
Um, San Francisco and

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.679
here in Olympic Valley.

00:02:42.519 --> 00:02:44.119
So excited to be back here.

00:02:50.039 --> 00:02:51.199
Ah, lots of ice.

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:53.039
Ah, here is less.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:02.079
We are at Auburn, endurance capital of

00:03:02.079 --> 00:03:04.519
the world, I call it.

00:03:04.519 --> 00:03:06.239
And here is the stadium.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.599
It is where Western

00:03:08.599 --> 00:03:11.719
States finish line is.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.599
And hopefully in one week I

00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:18.760
will enter this door here.

00:03:23.199 --> 00:03:25.159
To finish the race.

00:03:26.599 --> 00:03:28.239
And I'm going to run the

00:03:28.239 --> 00:03:32.519
last 20 miles of the race.

00:03:34.079 --> 00:03:37.559
Yeah, just to remember a bit how it looks

00:03:37.559 --> 00:03:38.800
like, how it feels like.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.960
I have a last

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.159
training day before the race.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:50.360
It's called now NN 202.

00:03:51.679 --> 00:03:53.519
It's a prototype that we have been

00:03:53.519 --> 00:03:56.559
working for doing like

00:03:56.559 --> 00:03:58.719
more long distance races.

00:03:59.719 --> 00:04:00.239
I have been running

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:02.360
like yeah, I think, yeah.

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:07.000
Probably like, I don't know,

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.679
700-800 kilometers on them.

00:04:09.679 --> 00:04:12.400
So, yeah, it's well tested though.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.679
Mile 99 flag.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.159
Last training before the race

00:04:50.159 --> 00:04:52.639
and yeah, it's feeling good.

00:04:52.639 --> 00:04:54.239
It's not super hot.

00:04:55.119 --> 00:04:55.880
So, it's a good

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:57.719
feeling to not feel too warm.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.519
And yeah, a big one on staurday

00:05:03.599 --> 00:05:05.920
Back to the track.

00:05:06.679 --> 00:05:07.639
Yeah, a bit excited.

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:10.400
I think we'll really come like probably

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.239
like Friday evening.

00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:13.000
Now it's kind of, yeah,

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:15.000
been there, been here.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.000
But yeah, it's nice to be back.

00:05:18.679 --> 00:05:20.119
So, yeah, now I just

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.679
need to rest as well.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:25.119
See how tomorrow feels, the TFL,

00:05:25.119 --> 00:05:26.280
but I think it's pretty okay.

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:30.000
So, I was measuring the sodium

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.119
concentration to see any day ratio like

00:05:33.119 --> 00:05:36.519
strategy during the race.

00:06:01.239 --> 00:06:03.280
those years were years of ambition.

00:06:04.559 --> 00:06:07.679
Prepairing all the food and we

00:06:07.679 --> 00:06:11.000
start like on the first hours with mix of

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.599
fats and some carbs like

00:06:13.599 --> 00:06:16.159
50-50 or even a little more.

00:06:16.519 --> 00:06:19.119
And then transitioning towards the end

00:06:19.119 --> 00:06:21.679
with it's more like fully carbs.

00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:24.440
So, it's kind of a transition from a mix

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:28.039
to when we are in a pace that is slow so

00:06:28.039 --> 00:06:30.480
we are not utilizing a lot of carbs

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.159
towards the end of the race where it will

00:06:32.159 --> 00:06:36.760
be more carb utilization and changing on

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:38.280
that through the race.

00:06:45.599 --> 00:06:47.400
Before they go to bed.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.679
Hey, hello.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.960
How do you feel?

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:58.400
Ah, good, yeah. It's very cold actually.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:01.000
Yes, I've heard

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.079
Yeah, yeah, it's like not even 30

00:07:03.079 --> 00:07:05.880
degrees. It looks like in Auburn.

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:09.840
And how do you, what will be your

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.199
strategy? Will you try to not

00:07:12.199 --> 00:07:14.000
let anyone escape this year?

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.840
Yeah, I will see because I

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:17.960
think in the uphills I can push.

00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.719
In the downhills I need to be very

00:07:21.719 --> 00:07:23.960
careful with the knee, I think

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.039
not to try to go too fast.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:26.760
So, probably will try to make it a bit

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:30.440
hard on the uphills and then down like to

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:33.599
be a bit more strategic

00:07:33.599 --> 00:07:35.880
and then see how I feel.

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.679
But yeah, I think it will be fast because

00:07:40.679 --> 00:07:42.079
it's cold so people are

00:07:42.079 --> 00:07:43.880
not really blowing up.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:47.400
I almost expected it warmer because if it's

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.320
harder I think it's better for me.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.039
It's exciting. It's 30 minutes to start

00:08:11.039 --> 00:08:15.760
and it's cold. It's a lot of wind so it

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:17.000
will be an interesting race.

00:08:17.399 --> 00:08:21.319
I'm feeling excited. These first four or

00:08:21.319 --> 00:08:23.960
five hours they are already like, you

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:25.920
want to get there because you are running

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:29.520
slow and it's nothing really happening.

00:08:30.239 --> 00:08:33.760
But yeah, excited to start

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.800
and to get to back to the mountains.

00:09:04.159 --> 00:09:06.720
Three, two, one.

